# Repo documentation

Read [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) and the matching `docs/apps/<name>.md` or `docs/packages/<name>.md` before editing.

## Expand when touched

If you make a **material** change (new routes, models, behavior, config) in a workspace whose doc is `Status: stub`, update that doc in the same change:

- Fill sections you relied on (Purpose, Entrypoints, Talks to, unknowns)
- Remove resolved items from **Out of scope / unknowns**
- Promote to `Status: deep` only when the page includes the deep sections (`Module map` / `Model map` + `Key flows`)

Skip doc updates for typo-only or purely cosmetic edits.

## Ownership

- `docs/` = source of truth for architecture
- `.cursor/rules/` = short conventions only — no long architecture prose
- App READMEs = pointer to `docs/` — no duplicate essays

Run `npm run check-docs` before finishing.
